Fix the default route, which the plugin asked for and then ignored.

route(8) into the jail was wrapped in `|| true`, so a failed add left the
container with an address, its segment and its own nameserver -- DNS answers --
and no way off the LAN, while the CNI result reported success and podman started
the container anyway. That is an outage which looks like a dead network: three
occurrences on our host before anything could even say so.

Instead: read the routing table back rather than trusting the exit status (`add`
prints "add net default: gateway X" even when it then fails, and a re-add over a
route somebody else installed answers EEXIST), retry, prefer `change` to
delete-then-add, and keep stderr in the log. cmd_check now reports a jail with no
default route, and the dhclient hook re-checks the route on every lease event
rather than only when the routers option changed -- routers almost never change,
a route going missing does.

